upcast — Views a value at one of the interfaces it implements.

Syntax:
  interface HasId {
    id: string
  }
  
  class User {
    implements HasId {
      id as user_id
    }
    full_name: string
    user_id: string
  }
  
  function label(user: User) -> string {
    return user.upcast<HasId>.id
  }

Use `value.upcast<Interface>` when a class implements multiple interfaces with the same member name or when you need the interface view. It takes one type argument and no call parentheses, as in `obj.upcast<I>.m()` and `self.upcast<I>.field`. The target must be an interface the value's type implements; the expression selects a contract and does not convert the value. Do not write `Type.upcast<Interface>` as a type; use `(Type as Interface).Assoc` for qualified associated type projection in a type position.
